Description: Converts written words into sequences of International
    Phonetic Alphabet phonemes for about 200 languages, using the
    spelling-to-sound rules of the Cross-linguistic Phonological Frequencies
    (XPF) corpus, Cohen Priva et al. (2021)
    <https://cohenpr-xpf.github.io/XPF/manual/xpf_manual.pdf>. The rules and
    the 'JavaScript' rule engine are bundled and run through 'V8', so no
    other software is needed. Each language comes with verification words
    that check its rules, and rules of your own can be loaded from 'JSON',
    'YAML' or legacy XPF files.
